WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.489 --> 00:00:04.890
Harry Potter fans have spent countless hours
mulling over the books and film franchise

00:00:04.890 --> 00:00:09.570
and have devised some pretty spellbinding
theories about the world of witchcraft and

00:00:09.570 --> 00:00:12.690
wizardry, some of which have even impressed
the author herself.

00:00:12.690 --> 00:00:15.999
Let's take a look at some of the most game-changing
of them all.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:17.640
Muggles vs. wizards

00:00:18.310 --> 00:00:23.120
Why do wizards have to hide their powers from
Muggles, and if they are so powerful, why

00:00:23.121 --> 00:00:25.050
aren't they in charge of the world?

00:00:25.050 --> 00:00:29.939
If history has taught us anything, it's that
usually those with superior firepower and

00:00:29.939 --> 00:00:32.099
knowledge win in any matchup.

00:00:32.099 --> 00:00:36.950
However, one Redditor had a different idea,
and it gives an interesting alternate explanation

00:00:36.950 --> 00:00:42.860
— Wizards and Muggles fought a war sometime
in the Middle Ages, and the Muggles won.

00:00:42.860 --> 00:00:47.630
In Goblet of Fire, it is revealed that the
Ministry of Magic has to talk to the British

00:00:47.630 --> 00:00:50.900
Prime Minister about bringing a dragon into
the country.

00:00:50.900 --> 00:00:55.590
This implies that the Minister of Magic reports
to the British Prime Minister and may require

00:00:55.590 --> 00:00:58.430
his approval for matters of this nature.

00:00:58.430 --> 00:01:02.620
Additionally, wizards of today appear to be
much less powerful when compared to ancient

00:01:02.620 --> 00:01:06.920
wizards like Merlin, the Peverells, and the
founders of Hogwarts.

00:01:06.920 --> 00:01:10.840
Perhaps the Muggles were more successful with
their trials and inquisitions than we were

00:01:10.840 --> 00:01:12.300
originally led to believe.

00:01:13.190 --> 00:01:14.880
The real Rita Skeeter

00:01:14.899 --> 00:01:19.421
There were a lot of colorful characters to
come and go in the Harry Potter series, but

00:01:19.421 --> 00:01:24.369
none felt quite as familiar as Rita Skeeter,
the intrepid journalist who would stop at

00:01:24.369 --> 00:01:26.499
nothing to get her scoop for the Daily Prophet.

00:01:26.499 --> 00:01:31.079
While her ethics were often questionable,
there was something about her prose that made

00:01:31.079 --> 00:01:32.939
many fans wonder whether J.K.

00:01:32.939 --> 00:01:37.149
Rowling may have designed the character to
be reminiscent of herself.

00:01:37.149 --> 00:01:42.229
After all, Rowling is also a writer who also
made a detailed accounting of the non-muggle

00:01:42.229 --> 00:01:45.960
world that feels very, very real to some readers.

00:01:45.960 --> 00:01:50.139
At least one theorist has taken it a step
further and suggested that Rowling actually

00:01:50.139 --> 00:01:55.619
is Rita Skeeter in real life, spilling all
of these well-documented details about the

00:01:55.619 --> 00:02:00.760
wizarding world to us no-maj types as a means
of getting revenge against those who shunned

00:02:00.760 --> 00:02:02.380
her from the other side.

00:02:02.380 --> 00:02:03.720
"Scratch that last."

00:02:05.460 --> 00:02:07.300
The secret of Horcruxes

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:12.720
One process that never gets fully explained
in the Harry Potter series is how horcruxes

00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:13.720
are made.

00:02:13.720 --> 00:02:18.000
Lord Voldemort was able to make himself a
bounty of these little life preservers at

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:22.660
some point in his younger years, but he seemed
to be the only one who ever had any backup

00:02:22.660 --> 00:02:27.390
souls to spare and seemed to be unable or
unwilling to create any more once our heroes

00:02:27.390 --> 00:02:30.220
started destroying them, so it must've been
difficult.

00:02:30.220 --> 00:02:33.430
"This is very dark stuff, very dark indeed."

00:02:33.430 --> 00:02:34.430
J.K.

00:02:34.430 --> 00:02:38.360
Rowling herself has been vague about how they're
made, though she did once say that attempts

00:02:38.360 --> 00:02:43.250
would probably be deadly for most wizards
because it's as complicated as splitting an

00:02:43.250 --> 00:02:44.250
atom.

00:02:44.250 --> 00:02:48.950
According to Harry Potter World UK on Twitter,
Rowling revealed the process to her editor

00:02:48.950 --> 00:02:51.720
who allegedly felt like vomiting after.

00:02:51.720 --> 00:02:55.840
This led one Redditor to surmise that cannibalism
may be involved.

00:02:55.840 --> 00:03:00.860
Both cannibalism and the creation of horcruxes
involve stealing a life force for the absorption

00:03:00.860 --> 00:03:01.860
of another.

00:03:01.860 --> 00:03:06.970
The theory seems to have gained some serious
traction in Fantastic Beasts: The Crimes of

00:03:06.970 --> 00:03:12.710
Grindelwald, as it was revealed that prior
to becoming Voldemort's pet and tag-along

00:03:12.710 --> 00:03:18.050
horcrux, Nagini was actually a shape-shifting
maledictus who had a female human form before

00:03:18.050 --> 00:03:20.580
we met her in the original series.

00:03:20.580 --> 00:03:24.440
Voldemort may have killed off the piece of
Nagini that was human and swapped in a piece

00:03:24.440 --> 00:03:25.940
of his own soul instead.

00:03:26.440 --> 00:03:28.800
In defense of the Dursleys

00:03:28.800 --> 00:03:34.070
When Voldemort tried to kill infant Harry,
a small piece of Tom Riddle's soul latched

00:03:34.070 --> 00:03:38.140
onto Harry's brain and cozied up in there
for the next 17 years.

00:03:38.140 --> 00:03:42.750
Even though Harry was not a "traditional"
Horcrux, we know that Voldemort's presence

00:03:42.750 --> 00:03:48.080
affected Harry, giving him some of Voldemort's
powers and causing occasional angry and violent

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:49.080
outbursts.

00:03:49.080 --> 00:03:53.210
What if Harry wasn't the only one affected
by Voldemort's presence?

00:03:53.210 --> 00:03:57.620
Voldemort's Horcruxes were capable of dramatically
changing the personality of someone exposed

00:03:57.620 --> 00:03:59.260
to one for extended periods.

00:03:59.260 --> 00:04:04.500
Harry and Hermione were frequently snappish
and angry while carrying the locket, and normally

00:04:04.500 --> 00:04:09.480
happy-go-lucky Ron turned into a raging, jealous
mess who abandoned his friends.

00:04:09.480 --> 00:04:15.130
If a Horcrux can do that to a genial and good-natured
person, what might it have done to the Dursleys,

00:04:15.130 --> 00:04:18.919
who were around Harry every day for ten years?

00:04:18.919 --> 00:04:23.410
From flashbacks, we know that Petunia wasn't
exactly a very nice person as a child, and

00:04:23.410 --> 00:04:25.380
Vernon was probably no better.

00:04:25.380 --> 00:04:30.840
But it is interesting to consider that maybe
their already sour natures were further exacerbated

00:04:30.840 --> 00:04:33.379
by Voldemort's evil influence.

00:04:33.379 --> 00:04:38.909
Since Dudley was born the same year as Harry,
he's literally lived almost his entire life

00:04:38.909 --> 00:04:40.449
around this Horcrux.

00:04:40.449 --> 00:04:43.300
It almost makes you feel a little sorry for
them.

00:04:43.300 --> 00:04:44.420
Almost.

00:04:48.540 --> 00:04:50.040
"Wake up, Potter!

00:04:50.040 --> 00:04:52.340
We're going to the zoo!"

00:04:53.040 --> 00:04:55.320
Neville's clumsiness

00:04:55.330 --> 00:05:00.639
During Neville Longbottom's first flying lesson
at Hogwarts, he earned a reputation as clumsy

00:05:00.639 --> 00:05:03.650
and perhaps not the brightest student in the
new class of first-years.

00:05:03.650 --> 00:05:08.180
There are plenty of other examples of Neville
being clumsy with magic and spells during

00:05:08.180 --> 00:05:12.030
his early years at the school, but that first
flying lesson may not have been Neville's

00:05:12.030 --> 00:05:13.419
fault at all.

00:05:13.419 --> 00:05:19.210
After Voldemort's death, the Longbottoms were
targeted by Death Eaters and tortured to insanity,

00:05:19.210 --> 00:05:24.039
which speaks to a definite animus against
the Longbottoms by Voldemort's crew.

00:05:24.039 --> 00:05:29.320
When Professor Quirrell first tries to kill
Harry in Sorcerer's Stone, he does so by bewitching

00:05:29.320 --> 00:05:32.919
Harry's broom as he rides it during a Quidditch
match.

00:05:32.919 --> 00:05:36.759
The unnatural movements of Harry's broom are
very similar to what happened to Neville during

00:05:36.759 --> 00:05:38.509
his flying lesson.

00:05:38.509 --> 00:05:43.199
What if that arm-breaking incident was because
Quirrell was using the same charm to exact

00:05:43.199 --> 00:05:45.660
a little torture on the Longbottom boy?

00:05:45.660 --> 00:05:49.529
It should also be pointed out that, until
it was broken during the events in Order of

00:05:49.529 --> 00:05:53.539
the Phoenix, Neville was using his father's
wand — the father who was driven insane

00:05:53.539 --> 00:05:55.180
when Neville was an infant.

00:05:55.180 --> 00:06:00.479
As we all know, "the wand chooses the wizard,"
and so some of Neville's early difficulties

00:06:00.479 --> 00:06:04.229
with spells may have been due to him using
this hand-me-down.

00:06:04.229 --> 00:06:08.490
After Neville gets a new wand, he seems to
grow in leaps and bounds in his confidence

00:06:08.490 --> 00:06:09.860
and spell abilities.

00:06:10.560 --> 00:06:12.360
Self-sorting wizards

00:06:12.370 --> 00:06:16.569
In Harry Potter and the Sorcerer's Stone,
the Sorting Hat struggles with where to put

00:06:16.569 --> 00:06:20.540
Potter, after the Boy Wizard kept thinking
over and over again:

00:06:21.100 --> 00:06:25.980
"Not Slytherin, not Slytherin."

00:06:25.999 --> 00:06:30.849
The Sorting Hat assured him that it'd be a
good fit for him but sent him over to Gryffindor

00:06:30.849 --> 00:06:32.930
instead, per his wishes.

00:06:32.930 --> 00:06:37.419
As a result of that scene, some fans suspect
that Harry may not have been the only one

00:06:37.419 --> 00:06:40.219
who moved himself to another house.

00:06:40.219 --> 00:06:44.910
One fan theory suggests that both Ron and
Hermione were also sent to Gryffindor rather

00:06:44.910 --> 00:06:49.520
than houses they were suited for — Hufflepuff
and Ravenclaw, respectively — because of

00:06:49.520 --> 00:06:51.150
their own preferences.

00:06:51.150 --> 00:06:55.620
For Ron, the reasoning behind the choice seems
simple enough; all of his family was already

00:06:55.620 --> 00:06:58.009
in Gryffindor, so he wanted to fit in.

00:06:58.009 --> 00:07:02.879
For Hermione, it may have been a reflection
of her own newfound valor in venturing into

00:07:02.880 --> 00:07:04.340
this whole new world alone.

00:07:04.760 --> 00:07:06.440
Centaurs know all

00:07:07.220 --> 00:07:11.599
There were two big scenes in the Harry Potter
series that pitted the titular wizard against

00:07:11.599 --> 00:07:16.279
his arch-nemesis Voldemort in the Forbidden
Forest, and the first may have foreshadowed

00:07:16.279 --> 00:07:17.599
the last.

00:07:17.599 --> 00:07:22.090
As one fan theorist points out, after his
brush with death as a baby, Harry's first

00:07:22.090 --> 00:07:26.110
encounter with the Dark Lord took place in
the forest, where he was sent to detention

00:07:26.110 --> 00:07:31.539
alongside Hermione, Ron and Draco Malfoy with
instructions to find out what was killing

00:07:31.539 --> 00:07:33.340
off the unicorns.

00:07:33.340 --> 00:07:37.979
There he found a cloaked figure, which he'd
later discover to be Voldemort, drinking a

00:07:37.979 --> 00:07:39.180
unicorn's blood.

00:07:39.180 --> 00:07:44.229
Firenze the centaur scared the figure away
and in the book was then scolded by his fellow

00:07:44.229 --> 00:07:46.289
centaur Bane, who warned him:

00:07:46.289 --> 00:07:49.869
"We are sworn not to set ourselves against
the heavens.

00:07:49.869 --> 00:07:53.259
Have we not read what is to come in the movements
of the planets?"

00:07:53.259 --> 00:07:57.120
The centaurs didn't go on to spell it out,
so what we didn't know at the time was that

00:07:57.120 --> 00:08:01.550
Harry's fate was to die at the hands of Voldemort
in that very place.

00:08:01.550 --> 00:08:05.851
The centaurs pretty much foretold the final
battle before Harry knew the identity of the

00:08:05.851 --> 00:08:08.750
cloaked figure that threatened his life so
early on.

00:08:08.750 --> 00:08:11.380
"Just something to think about."

00:08:12.080 --> 00:08:13.480
Protecting Snape

00:08:14.040 --> 00:08:18.760
The Defense Against the Dark Arts classroom
was a revolving door for professors at Hogwarts

00:08:18.779 --> 00:08:20.689
during Harry's time as a student.

00:08:20.689 --> 00:08:25.319
First, there was a Professor Quirrell, who
carried Voldemort on the back of his head;

00:08:25.319 --> 00:08:30.290
then came Gilderoy Lockhart, who was a fraud
and lost all his memories due to a misfired

00:08:30.290 --> 00:08:31.490
memory charm.

00:08:31.490 --> 00:08:36.579
Remus Lupin also walked away after he was
exposed as a werewolf, then Mad-Eye Moody

00:08:36.579 --> 00:08:41.729
turned out to be Barty Crouch Jr. in disguise,
and Dolores Umbridge got herself dismissed

00:08:41.729 --> 00:08:46.490
for insubordination and general wickedness
before Severus Snape was finally transferred

00:08:46.490 --> 00:08:49.380
from his position as Potions professor to
take over.

00:08:49.740 --> 00:08:55.380
"You know, I really hate children."

00:08:55.380 --> 00:08:59.399
All the while, Snape seemed like the most
obvious choice for the role, and some fans

00:08:59.399 --> 00:09:04.290
were left to wonder why he didn't get it until
Harry Potter and the Half-Blood Prince.

00:09:04.290 --> 00:09:07.959
One theory has it that Dumbledore never gave
him the post to protect him.

00:09:07.959 --> 00:09:13.070
The idea is that because he wouldn't let Tom
Riddle have the job years before, Riddle cursed

00:09:13.070 --> 00:09:17.640
the position and assured that everyone who
occupied it would suffer some kind of cruel

00:09:17.640 --> 00:09:20.730
fate and serve just one year.

00:09:20.730 --> 00:09:24.699
Dumbledore refused Snape the job until he
made the Unbreakable Vow to kill Dumbledore

00:09:24.699 --> 00:09:27.649
and thus resigned himself to a horrible year
already.

00:09:27.649 --> 00:09:33.120
The theory might also explain why Snape, as
Headmaster, installed a death eater in the

00:09:33.120 --> 00:09:37.730
role next, as he was clearly willing to sabotage
the guy on the sly whenever possible.

00:09:37.730 --> 00:09:42.430
"Are you incapable of restraining yourself
or do you take pride in being an insufferable

00:09:42.430 --> 00:09:43.740
know-it-all?"

00:09:44.140 --> 00:09:46.480
Professor Trelawney was the real deal

00:09:46.780 --> 00:09:51.060
She might have caught a lot of flak for her
histrionics, but Professor Trelawney was actually

00:09:51.079 --> 00:09:54.649
on the mark with her prophecies a lot more
often than people thought.

00:09:54.649 --> 00:09:59.420
For example, a re-read of what she predicted
in Harry Potter and the Prisoner of Azkaban

00:09:59.420 --> 00:10:03.269
has some theorists believing she predicted
Dumbledore's death long before it happened

00:10:03.269 --> 00:10:06.380
because she refused a seat at Christmas dinner
by saying:

00:10:06.380 --> 00:10:09.730
"If I join the table, we shall be thirteen!

00:10:09.730 --> 00:10:11.620
Nothing could be more unlucky!

00:10:11.620 --> 00:10:17.460
Never forget that when thirteen dine together,
the first to rise will be the first to die!"

00:10:17.460 --> 00:10:22.910
With Peter Pettigrew hiding out in the form
of Ron's rat Scabbers, there were 13 people

00:10:22.910 --> 00:10:26.779
at the table, and Dumbledore was the first
to stand.

00:10:26.779 --> 00:10:30.899
Meanwhile, she might not have been so wrong
in Harry Potter and the Goblet of Fire when

00:10:30.899 --> 00:10:33.850
she sensed that Harry was born in "mid-winter."

00:10:33.850 --> 00:10:38.081
Harry was a July baby, but what we didn't
know at the time was that a piece of Voldemort

00:10:38.081 --> 00:10:43.620
was still embedded in him, and Tom Riddle's
birthday just so happened to be December 31st.

00:10:43.620 --> 00:10:47.399
Some speculate her misinterpretation may have
only been due to the fact that her sense was

00:10:47.399 --> 00:10:52.029
so strong that she was picking up on the Dark
Lord's date of birth instead.

00:10:52.029 --> 00:10:55.910
It looks like Sybill Trelawney shouldn't have
been such a laughingstock after all.

